{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/108655-need-ideas-for-social-or-mental-challenges","id":108655,"title":"Need ideas for social or mental challenges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-08T15:28:55-07:00","id":108655,"title":"Need ideas for social or mental challenges","content":"I'm continuing with my Scion game after a year long break but there are going to be some changes. The reason why we took a break is because I and my fianc\u00e9e (who is also one of the players) were blessed with a baby girl one year ago and we had to take a short break. This break got longer when we realized that a game with 6 players would simply be too much for the little one, and even a group of 4 players progresses slowly with a baby around (both because of the 'awww'-factor and the 'wahh'-factor). So I've decided to split the group in two.<br /> <br /> When we left the game a year ago, things were heating up between the Aesir and the Atzl\u00e1nti, especially after Odin and Tezcatlipoca pretty much levelled a noticable part of London during a dispute. Essentially, there is going to be war and the Gods are picking sides. On one side, we have the PCs from the Aesir, Amatsukami and the Yazata, and on the other we have the PCs from the Atzl\u00e1nti, Dodekatheon and T\u00faatha de Danaan. The reason why the PCs a split this way has to do with their strong points. The latter group includes physically powerful characters, able to take on big baddies and wrestle them down. The others are more social and two of the players prefer not to participate much in combat. The third is focusing his character to be more of a sneaky type.<br /> <br /> As you may have noticed, I'm not really focusing this campaign on the Titanomachy. Titans are cool, in a way, although I made some changes to them, but I wanted to focus this on the Gods and the pantheon relations. Currently, they've realized that Pan was trying to start a war between the Gods (in an attempt to destroy the Dodekatheon, particularly Apollo), so he is a figure in this, although he is less of a pawn for the Titans and more of a mastermind (or possibly manipulated by some other force).<br /> <br /> The campaign idea also assumes that each Scion increases their Legend between stories, so there are no small stories. There are some side-stories, sure, but the main story is always something huge or has a large impact. For the physical group, I intend for them to go against Pan, but I'm unsure about the others. The idea was to have them seek out three personal items from three Gods, one from each pantheon. It sounds a bit small, but the items I had in mind are the hair of Raiden, the blood of Vahram and the semen of Odin (possibly something more if it turns out to be too easy). While doing this, they also have to find a Scion of Heimdall in order to take his father's place before the Ragnarok comes (admittedly, this story will focus somewhat on the Aesir). I imagine, later on, that getting one pantheon to join the side of the Aesir is going to be the focus on one of the stories but I need some more ideas.<br /> <br /> What ideas can you give me to challenge mentally and socially adept Scions of upper demi-god, and possibly god, tier (they're already Legend 7)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T03:06:43-07:00","id":110673,"title":"","content":"No ideas then? Not one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T04:09:37-07:00","id":110699,"title":"","content":"Social? Rock off. Have each pantheon put together a band and have a battle of the bands. Scions should be able to make some earth-shattering music. Less musically inclined scions can help with things like special effects, nothing like a literal earthquake to compliment a drum solo. I'll get back to you later kinda tired right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T07:47:21-07:00","id":110787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/108655-need-ideas-for-social-or-mental-challenges?p=110699#post110699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social? Rock off. Have each pantheon put together a band and have a battle of the bands. Scions should be able to make some earth-shattering music. Less musically inclined scions can help with things like special effects, nothing like a literal earthquake to compliment a drum solo. I'll get back to you later kinda tired right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not completely related, but I found it awesome anyway: In the campaign I was in, we needed all of creation to weep at the same time for Baldur in order to bring him back to life. So our science-y based scion turned Yggdrassil into a giant speaker that could broadcast everywhere all at once. She also invented a target that was able to convert the strikes from Mjolnir into useable energy to power the rig. Then my character, a jazz/blues singer, created a really soulful song about Baldur which was then sent out by the world tree to all points. <br /> <br /> A concert helped turn the tide of Ragnarok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T07:52:04-07:00","id":110790,"title":"","content":"Music really does fit with epic anything so very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}